1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 c6 5. h4 h5 6. Qd2 b5 7. Bd3 Nd7 8. Nh3
Ngf6 9. Ng5 Ng4 10. f4 Qb6 11. Ne2 e5 12. c3 Nxe3 13. Qxe3 Nf6 14. fxe5 dxe5
15. O-O-O Ng4 16. Qg3 O-O 17. Bc2 a5 18. Rhf1 a4 19. b4 f6 20. Nf3 Be6 21. Kb1
Rad8 22. Nh2 Kh7 23. d5 Bc8 ({One can understand why Kurajica did not choose
to annotate this game for us. But why doesn't} 23... Nxh2 {win a pawn?" 
(Reuben)}) 24. Nxg4 Bxg4 25. Qf2 Qc7 26. Rfe1 cxd5 27. exd5 f5 28. Qc5 Qb7 29.
Qc6 Qxc6 30. dxc6 Rxd1+ 31. Bxd1 Rc8 32. c4 Rxc6 33. c5 Rc8 34. Nc3 e4 35. Kc2
Bxc3 36. Kxc3 Rd8 37. Be2 Bxe2 38. Rxe2 Rd3+ 39. Kb2 g5 40. c6 Rd8 41. g3 Rc8
42. Rc2 gxh4 43. gxh4 f4 44. Kc1 e3 45. Rc3 f3 46. Rxe3 Rxc6+ 47. Kd2 Rf6 48.
Ke1 Rf4 49. a3 Kg6 50. Kf2 Rxh4 51. Rxf3 Rh2+ 52. Ke3 Rb2 53. Kd4 Rg2 54. Kc5
Rg5+ 55. Kc6 h4 56. Rf8 h3 57. Rf3 h2 58. Rh3 Rh5 59. Rxh2 Rxh2 60. Kxb5 Kf6
61. Kxa4 Ke6 62. Kb5 Kd6 63. a4 Rh5+ 64. Kb6 Rh4 65. Kb5 Kc7 66. a5 Kb7 67. a6+
Ka7 68. Ka5 Rh8 {"We have devised a new I. Q. test around Bojan's score sheets.
They are almost completely illegible. Last year I handed one over to Kenny
Harman for interpretation. He came back with a perfectly reasonable game,
bearing little or no resemblance to that actually played! He is not by any
means the only offender, perhaps next year we will offer a prize for the best
score sheets. I think the following is correct. Anyway it is one of the most
interesting games that I have made up otherwise." (Reuben) Source: The
Islingtonian No. 11 (1968/9)} 0-1

